WEBVTT

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:06.640
Lupin!

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.150
Lupin!

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.320
The border patrol.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.300
Inspector, you have to come back!

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.220
Unhand me, Yata!

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.310
I'm still off-duty!

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.290
Let's go, Zenigata.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.790
Lupin's dead. Now, it's up to us
 to do what only we can do.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.670
If anything happens to me...

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.250
...can you look after the girl?

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.060
That damned idiot...

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.400
I'm going to do...

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.220
...something only I can do.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.910
<b>A Crook's Resolve</b>

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:25.330
<i>And once again, I'm no longer 
my wife's favorite male in her life.</i>

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.710
<i>Now, she's crazy about Ricky, 
the search-and-rescue dog!</i>

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.160
<i>The whole world's going to join hands!</i>

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:32.500
<i>Just like this.</i>

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:36.680
<i>More news now on the recent 
dismantling of an art forgery ring...</i>

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:41.280
<i>The chief of the French Central Directorate 
of the Judicial Police, Albert d'Andrésy,</i>

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.390
<i>has said his organization's collaboration with</i>

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.350
Say...

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.440
<i>the General Directorate for Internal Security</i>

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:48.330
Do you remember that game everyone 
was going nuts over a while back?

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.550
<i>was key to the success of the investigation.</i>

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.430
Which one?

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:52.170
You know, the one about catching that thief.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.560
Oh, that one. I think it ended when 
the thief was killed, didn't it?

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.940
Do you remember his name?

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:02.900
No...

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:06.370
I think it was something 
Asian-sounding, wasn't it?

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.720
That's what I thought.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:16.560
Inspector Zenigata, you're going to 
be working narcotics from now on.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.210
That's not fair, sir!

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.350
The inspector was just 
trying to arrest Lupin—

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.880
And it was broadcast to the entire world.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.720
He was seen assisting a known criminal.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:29.780
You've been chasing Lupin all 
this time, but now, he's dead.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.850
Enough is enough.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.360
I understand, sir.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.060
I-Inspector Zenigata!

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:49.670
You've moved departments?

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.640
Yeah. I'm working narcotics now.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.960
Lupin's not dead.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.390
I haven't seen his body.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:09.210
Say, Zenigata...

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:15.590
This pasta called "soba" is pretty good! Yeah...

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:18.230
You think so? Glad you like it!

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.530
<b>Zenigata</b>

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:22.790
I'm heading out.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.480
Have a safe trip.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:28.780
What is it?

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.820
Is this really necessary?

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.300
Routines are important!

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:35.680
You stay at my place, 
you play by my rules.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.200
Hello, Underworld.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.430
Verify session information from crawl.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.800
Check stacks.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:55.810
Once indexing is complete, run a search.
 Check all unique passwords.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.830
Activate IP camera network.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.830
<b>To 
Amy</b>

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.520
<i>I am here to deliver a message.</i>

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:20.840
<b>Marco Polo's up again</b>

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:20.840
<b>I know their system was attacked</b>

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.920
<b>Back online for a day and 
we make over 2 mill in sales. 
Even if we had to take some 
risks to get up and running 
again...</b>

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.430
<b>Seems like it was 
worth it, after all</b>

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:28.430
<b>Don't celebrate just yet</b>

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.850
<b>We're still in the red</b>

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:32.930
<b>The longer we stayed shut 
down, the more customers 
we would've lost.</b>

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.930
<b>It's a gamble, but
a necessary one</b>

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:37.440
<b>And we've already won</b>

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.860
<b>At this rate, we'll have 
recovered our losses 
within a year</b>

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:40.520
<b>Don't celebrate just yet</b>

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.860
<b>Seems like it was worth it, after all</b>

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.860
<b>We're still in the red</b>

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.860
<b>The longer we were shut down,</b>

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.950
<b>I just got a message from 
someone interesting</b>

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:47.860
<b>Lemme forward it 
to you guys</b>

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.130
"Underworld"?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.700
<b>This is probably whoever 
set up that backdoor</b>

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.000
<b>What do they want now?</b>

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:57.830
<b>I'll go meet them</b>

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:58.830
<b>Don't be stupid</b>

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.210
<b>You can do whatever, 
but count me out</b>

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.000
<b>What the hell are you
 thinking, Peeca Boo?</b>

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:02.380
<b>What the hell are you
 thinking, Peeca Boo?</b>

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.510
<b>I wanna try something 
I saw in a movie once</b>

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.250
<b>Check it out</b>

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.710
<b>This girl has to be
Underworld</b>

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:43.130
<b>Be careful</b>

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.590
<b>Nothing's certain yet</b>

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:51.580
<i>Welcome to Marco Polo's castle!</i>

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:59.140
Castle? Seems more like an amusement park.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.230
<i>So just how crazy are you?</i>

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.870
Wanting to work for us, I mean...

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:09.160
<i>I can turn the Marco Polo website 
into something a bit less shoddy.</i>

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:12.250
<i>You've seen how scary getting 
hacked can be, haven't you?</i>

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:14.340
You've got the nerve to ask me that question?

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.110
Who better to ask it than me?

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:20.990
<i>Have a seat.</i>

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.490
<i>Don't expect anything to drink, though.</i>

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:29.740
Why is there only one seat?

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.000
The deal was to meet face-to-face.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.300
You seriously think 
we're on even terms here?

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.810
<i>Do you think I made only one backdoor?</i>

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.110
Threats, huh? Well, in that case...

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:02.690
I thought stuff like this 
only happened in movies.

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:07.060
<i>Same here. But I wanted 
to give it a try for real.</i>

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:08.530
This makes you the bad guy, you realize?

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:11.200
We've both been "bad guys" from the beginning.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.300
You're a hacker, and I'm a drug dealer.

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:15.570
<i>Let me get to the point.</i>

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:17.400
<i>Tell me about Lupin's collection.</i>

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.900
Is that why you agreed to meet me?

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:22.310
<i>You hung around with Lupin for a bit.</i>

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.390
<i>Hideouts, passwords... 
Tell me everything you saw.</i>

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:29.460
<i>We're going to take back everything 
he took from us, and then some.</i>

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:34.140
<i>Don't expect the water to 
suddenly stop rising, either.</i>

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:35.940
<i>I'm the crook, after all.</i>

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:41.450
<i>When I first touched 
a computer, I was so excited...</i>

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:45.770
<i>I could go anywhere and meet anyone.</i>

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:47.750
<i>It felt like my horizons had suddenly expanded.</i>

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:48.700
I know what she means.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:52.210
That's how I felt when 
I got my first motorbike...

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.110
I got praise for the code I wrote.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:57.400
From all over the world.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:01.170
And people stopped treating me like a child.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.230
<b>Peeca Boo, how long are you going 
to let this monologue drone on for?</b>

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:07.330
<i>I was able to get information, 
money, and security with ease.</i>

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.590
I don't want your life story!

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.470
Tell me about Lupin!

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:14.990
<i>After a while, it stopped being exciting.</i>

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:18.230
<i>But I didn't have the courage 
to break the status quo.</i>

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:22.820
That's when <i>he</i> showed up from the 
hellhole I called "the real world."

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:27.060
And I decided to accept 
his invitation to go outside.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:29.610
<i>Tell me about Lupin!</i>

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.180
<i>Why do women insist on babbling 
about junk that doesn't matter?</i>

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:35.520
But the real world was every bit 
as crappy as I thought it would be.

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:38.120
<i>Inconvenient, unpleasant, 
oppressively hot...</i>

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.260
<i>Not to mention, dangerous.</i>

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.520
Drop the tough girl act already!

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:42.230
You're gonna die, bitch!

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:44.920
But... it was exciting!

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:47.770
It gave me the best high I'd ever had!

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:55.270
That idiot! Why'd she have to be stubborn?!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.880
Why are you calling me?

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:02.200
<i>Is your real name Chuck Glay?</i>

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:05.310
<i>Because our pics were just 
posted on Happy Deathday!</i>

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:06.740
<i>All three of us! With our real names!</i>

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:07.530
What?!

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.420
<b>Look at the bounty</b>

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.420
<b>It's the same amount 
Lupin stole from us</b>

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.070
But Lupin's dead!

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:19.980
<i>His friends must've done it!</i>

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:20.570
Shit...

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:22.120
Then, we'll beat them at their own game.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:24.490
Put Jigen and Goemon on there!

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:25.260
<i>It'll make no difference!</i>

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:28.070
<i>Even if we do that, our names 
will still be on the site!</i>

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:39.420
What's going on?!

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:40.570
Hey, Chap!

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:47.040
<b>I just heard a gunshot</b>

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:47.780
Is it... an assassin?

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:47.910
<b>I'm out for now</b>

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:53.840
<b>See ya</b>

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.890
Damn it! Don't you dare!

00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:53.340
<i>Sounds like the hitmen 
have already found you.</i>

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.270
The hell is this?! How can you still talk?

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:02.210
<i>If you're curious, why don't
 you come down here?</i>

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:07.930
<i>Let's make a deal. I can take 
your name off that website.</i>

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:09.850
You think I'd believe you?

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.720
<i>You think you have a choice?</i>

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:17.600
<i>First, we meet in person. We can 
discuss the particulars afterwards.</i>

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:23.790
You're serious about being able 
to get my name taken down, right?

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:27.040
<i>I hacked it before when I was trying 
to get Lupin's name removed.</i>

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.050
<i>I just didn't get there in time in his case.</i>

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:33.250
Fine. You get my name off 
there, and I'll help you.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.750
<i>"Help"?</i>

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.520
<i>I'm pretty sure </i>I'm<i> the one helping </i>you<i>.</i>

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.240
<i>We're equals in this deal.</i>

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:40.970
I get it.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.040
I'll pick my words more 
carefully from now on.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:46.230
It's open...

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:52.270
I'm here, Underworld!

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:54.890
Now, help us!

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:01.160
No way...

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.960
Lupin III?!

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:17.710
Impossible!

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:22.990
You're... supposed to be dead!

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:24.260
And...

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:28.970
It's just an AR filter.

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:32.980
I knew all about your dorky little trap.

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:37.480
So I made sure there was a way out, 
and got Amy to whip up a watery AR filter.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:43.240
<b>To 
Amy</b>

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:46.240
I get it!

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.110
You're alive because—

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:50.070
Kinda slow to catch on, aren't you?

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:53.750
That drone was ours all along.

00:12:56.770 --> 00:13:01.970
Amy used AR to make it look like 
I was dead to everyone watching.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:05.460
Standing in the right spot to match 
the filter was a real pain, though.

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:09.750
You've been dancing to my 
tune this entire time.

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:13.860
Fujiko was meant to be 
the one to make the kill,

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:17.490
but Old Man Zenigata's intervention meant 
there were a few alterations to the plan.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.800
That bastard Lupin...

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.650
The whole time he was in Bwanda...

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:28.550
He had us figured out!

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.900
You're not going anywhere, kid.

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:51.500
Bye-bye, you two.

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:53.200
It was fun while it lasted.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.040
Move an inch and I strike.

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:03.520
We have your partners' locations as well.

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:06.940
Jigen and Goemon are putting 
them in a timeout as we speak.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:12.790
Your gun's not a toy, right?

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:23.030
Ready to play a game where 
it's <i>your </i>life on the line?

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:32.130
Because if you don't have the guts 
to do so, you shouldn't be a crook.

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:35.560
You should choose the safe life, obeying
 the rules that others have made for you.

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:44.390
Here it comes...

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:46.060
That's far enough, Lupin!

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.110
Pops? But how?

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:52.110
I left him a note.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:54.110
Excuse me? Why would you—

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:54.740
Lupin...

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:58.730
Shoot him and you'll get 
sent down for murder.

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:01.670
You're not even a little surprised 
about the fact I'm alive?

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:04.950
Did you seriously think I wouldn't 
catch on to your little scheme...

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:06.490
when I saw it play out in front of my eyes?

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:10.260
And here I was thinking the smoke 
would've made a difference...

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:12.830
Hang on a tick, pal.

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:14.960
We're not done chatting.

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:17.620
This old guy right here is 
Zenigata from the ICPO.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:19.480
That makes him the enemy of every crook.

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:24.640
What's the call? You could always 
turn yourself in, instead.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:28.620
Cough up enough info and they might 
even keep you safe for a decade...

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:29.540
...behind bars.

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:34.380
Time to choose: your life? Or your freedom?

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:35.540
Five...

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:37.800
Four...

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:39.790
Three...

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:42.080
Two...

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:43.850
One—

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:45.290
Save me!

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:56.010
T-Take me in, Inspector!

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:59.060
I was selling drugs on the 
internet! So, please...

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:01.060
And you'll testify to that?

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:03.550
Anything you want! Please!

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:05.560
All right.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:08.930
Looks like you were never a match for me.

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:15.020
See ya, Pops!

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:18.910
Hold it! Lupin! Amy!

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:20.920
It's Ami.

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:23.050
Zenigata... Thank you.

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:33.960
No need to thank me, kid.

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.950
Don't leave me alone!

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:38.530
I'm begging you!

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:40.820
We're gonna have a nice <i>long </i>chat!

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:44.420
After all, narcotics are my thing right now.

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:56.430
It's done.

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:58.990
<i>Calling to thank me?</i>

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:01.060
<i>Just giving you the heads-up.</i>

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:03.020
<i>This was business.</i>

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:05.750
Even though you turned to 
me in your hour of need?

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:10.290
Well, out of all the women I know, 
no one can lie quite like you.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.500
<i>Seems like a bit of gratitude 
wouldn't go amiss...</i>

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:17.760
You already got the bounty 
from Happy Deathday, didn't you?

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.610
<i>Miss Drone Fighter.</i>

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:21.590
I suppose so.

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:24.520
Payment was received, as promised.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:28.100
The job is done.

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:31.510
No reason... to keep talking, then.

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:37.950
Yeah. There's nothing to say.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:41.910
<i>Well... Not between us, anyway.</i>

00:18:02.530 --> 00:18:04.500
It's no problem at all.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:06.520
You're regulars, and I know you both.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:07.670
Here.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:09.510
Thank you so much.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:12.280
This old coot's gone senile, I tell you.

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:14.780
You're the one who forgot the pepper.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.530
No, it was you!

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:19.260
The people from upstairs?

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:25.250
Yeah. They hadn't come down here in a while, 
so I was a little worried about them.

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:30.970
Zenigata has been allowed to return 
to his previous department.

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:35.910
Yeah. Apparently, that was his reward 
for bringing down Marco Polo.

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:38.290
Guess I'm back to playing 
hide-and-seek with Pops.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:40.690
What a pain in the neck!

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:46.350
I must say, this massive pot 
of shabu-shabu is delicious.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.360
It's cheese fondue, man!

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:51.040
By the way, where's Ami?

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:52.320
She's at school.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.410
A boarding school, that is.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.710
Think you can make it on your own?

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:08.920
I don't know.

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:10.170
Come now...

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.240
But I'm excited.

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.260
I see. Well, that's good.

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:22.870
Yeah.

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:31.240
Hey, Lupin, remember when I asked 
you why you don't just retire?

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:32.370
Yeah.

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:35.760
You've stolen enough money to live in the
 lap of luxury for the rest of your life, right?

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:38.280
And it's not like you're obsessed with art.

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.360
No shortage of ladies, either.

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:45.120
I've been wondering this whole 
time why you'd keep doing...

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:47.120
something as dangerous as being a thief...

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:49.610
And what's your diagnosis, doc?

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:05.870
Because it's exciting.

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.670
You should've seen the look on her face.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:37.500
Anyway, I wanted to run something 
interesting by you two.

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:42.560
Is that Spain? The map's reversed, though.

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:44.220
Let's hear it.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.010
Yeah.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:48.460
You're gonna find this one 
pretty exciting, guys.

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:17.110
I'm Fujiko Mine.

00:22:17.430 --> 00:22:19.850
Our target this time is a smart safe!

00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:23.980
It has a feature that lets it analyze 
the performance of a human brain.

00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:22.570
<b>POWER</b>

00:22:23.980 --> 00:22:27.710
The smarter you are, 
the harder it is to open!

00:22:27.710 --> 00:22:30.980
Wait a sec. How's Lupin going to open it?

00:22:30.980 --> 00:22:34.200
How does a genius rid himself of his genius?

00:22:30.990 --> 00:22:32.740
<b>Wisdom</b>

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:37.240
Looks like this is going 
to take some work, Lupin.

00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:40.890
Next time: Lupin vs. the Smart Safe.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:45.000
<b>Lupin vs. the Smart Safe</b>

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:44.150
I hope you're ready for this one, Lupin.
